id: interface/source-bound-yawnbot-workbench-v0.1
title: "Source-bound Yawnbot workbench"
kind: interface-contract
status: working-draft-0.1
version: 0.1.0-draft
updated: 2026-09-01

purpose: >
  Let a person place an unrestricted source or thought into a Yawnbot, inspect
  how the system is interpreting it, correct the emerging model, provision
  useful expressions, and follow movement through reality without making the
  person complete an ontology form or mistaking a polished View for truth.

one_model_rule: >
  This is a noncanonical View over core/source-bound-mental-model.yawn, the
  Orientation Map, Agency Holarchy, inquiry selection, Move selection, proof,
  and audience-policy records. It does not create another cognition store,
  runtime Agent identity, authority source, or master loop.

entry:
  routes:
    generic: /new
    account_scoped_example: /dave/new
  prompt: "What has your attention?"
  accepted_inputs:
    - typed or spoken thought
    - pasted text
    - conversation or transcript reference
    - document or artifact reference
    - image or event reference
    - existing .yawn coordinate
  source_rule: >
    Preserve or reference the submitted source before proposing segmentation,
    labels, Questions, characters, claims, relationships, or Moves. When exact
    bytes are unavailable, show reference-only and integrity status instead of
    inventing a content hash.

progressive_resolution:
  initial_surface:
    - source signal
    - proposed Yawnbot name and coordinate
    - one governing Question candidate
    - privacy state
    - confirm, correct, reject, add more, defer, and inspect-source controls
  rule: >
    Ask only the few Questions most likely to change a rightful next choice.
    Never require all cells to be filled, and never use completeness as a score
    of intelligence, worth, consciousness, honesty, maturity, or readiness.

workbench_cells:
  - id: source
    label: Source
    maps_to: [sourceRecords, compilerProposals]
  - id: relationship
    label: Relationship
    maps_to: [relationshipRef, arenaRef, relations]
  - id: questions
    label: Questions
    maps_to: [questions]
  - id: positions
    label: Answers
    canonical_label: Positions
    maps_to: [positions]
  - id: facets
    label: Model
    maps_to: [modelFacets, characterViews]
  - id: expressions
    label: Expressions
    maps_to: [expressionProvisions, projections]
  - id: moves
    label: Moves
    maps_to: [moves]
  - id: reality
    label: Reality
    maps_to: [consequences]
  - id: evaluations
    label: Judgments
    canonical_label: Evaluations
    maps_to: [evaluations]
  - id: proof
    label: Proof
    maps_to: [proofAdjudications, updates]
  - id: access
    label: Access
    maps_to: [audiencePolicies, runtimeBinding, boundary]

cell_states:
  allowed:
    - unknown
    - proposed
    - reported
    - accepted_as_attributed
    - disputed
    - blocked
    - stale
    - evidence_pending
    - evidenced
    - unauthorized
  rules:
    - "Unknown and held states remain visible and are not failures."
    - "Reported, inferred, proposed, accepted-as-attributed, and proved remain visually distinct."
    - "A populated cell is not necessarily true, current, relevant, consented, or authorized."
    - "Only attributed records determine state; the renderer never promotes canonical state."

passage_view:
  label: "Follow this Yawn"
  canonical: false
  default_order:
    - Question
    - Position
    - Expression provision
    - Projection
    - Move
    - Consequence
    - Evaluation
    - Proof adjudication
    - Update
    - Question
  rendering_rule: >
    Render only records that exist. Branch whenever multiple Questions,
    Positions, Moves, Consequences, or Evaluations coexist. Show holds and
    missing stages rather than drawing a false completed line. Selecting any
    stage opens its source, attribution, relations, alternatives, confidence,
    audience, authority, and revision history.

compiler_feed:
  units:
    - source segment
    - proposed thought or cognitive facet
    - proposed Question
    - proposed Position
    - proposed relation or coupling
    - proposed character View
    - proposed expression provision
    - proposed Move
    - explicit lacuna or conflict
  operations: [confirm, reject, correct, add_more, defer, inspect_sources]
  effect: proposal-only
  boundary: >
    Confirming records that the representation is acceptable for the stated
    scope. It does not prove the claim, authorize a Move, activate an Agent,
    widen access, or publish anything.

expression_panel:
  definition: >
    An expression provision chooses purpose, audience, interface mode,
    Questions, Positions, aperture, constraints, and allowed Projection kinds.
  examples:
    - explain
    - concise update
    - founder letter
    - research paper
    - timeline
    - lesson
    - debate
    - relationship conversation
    - Nestheads game View
  rule: >
    A preview remains a draft Projection. An expression event is recorded only
    when an attributed Projection actually enters its Arena.

judgment_panel:
  user_label: Judgment
  canonical_record: Evaluation
  must_show:
    - evaluator
    - target
    - phase
    - relationship and Arena
    - criteria snapshot and basis
    - criterion-level judgments
    - overall assessment
    - sources and evidence
    - confidence and epistemic status
    - dissenting Evaluations
    - Questions opened
  primary_prompt: "According to what?"
  boundary: >
    Reality returns Consequences; an evaluator supplies Judgment. Neither a
    strong feeling nor an authoritative voice may silently convert Evaluation
    into Consequence, proof, choice, permission, or identity.

character_layer:
  default: optional
  rule: >
    A Nestheads or other character may represent a facet, Question, tension,
    relationship, or passage for memorability and play. Show which records the
    character represents. Do not give it Agent status, persistence, authority,
    or a profile merely because it appears animate.

access_panel:
  operations:
    - keep private
    - share with named audience
    - propose public View
    - request affected-principal consent
    - configure redaction
    - allow or disallow access requests
    - inspect authorization and revocation
  boundary: >
    "Must expose to the network" is a disclosure-requirement proposal, not a
    publication event. Connection never widens visibility, imports truth, or
    transfers authority by inheritance.

portable_connection:
  user_language: "Connect this Yawnbot"
  creates: >
    A typed, scoped, attributed, revocable relationship edge between stable
    coordinates or package revisions.
  never_creates:
    - merged identity
    - inherited agreement
    - inherited consent
    - inherited privacy aperture
    - inherited authority
    - imported proof

kickstarter_dogfood:
  coordinate: dave/kickstarter/nestheads
  default_expression: founder-update
  current_visible_state:
    source: reference-only
    governing_question: proposed
    positions: proposed
    founder_message: draft
    send_move: proposed
    consequence: absent
    evaluation: proposed
    proof: absent
    public_access: candidate-not-authorized
  character_use: >
    Existing Nestheads assets may render context, shame, accountability,
    assumptions, and lacunae after an asset manifest and owner-reviewed mapping
    are approved. The base View must remain usable without animation or game art.

illegal_casts:
  - "cell completion -> truth or worth"
  - "Answer label -> canonical truth"
  - "expression configuration -> expression event"
  - "preview -> sent message"
  - "expected result -> Consequence"
  - "Judgment -> reality or proof"
  - "accept proposal -> publish"
  - "connect -> inherit"
  - "character -> Agent"
  - "passage View -> ontology"

implementation_boundary:
  current: protocol-only
  not_authorized:
    - production UI change
    - database migration
    - private source import
    - model call
    - character generation
    - message send
    - public publication
    - runtime Agent activation
    - external effect

proof:
  required_scenarios:
    - messy self-reflection transcript
    - consciousness Question with several Positions
    - founder-accountability draft with no send receipt
    - conflicting Evaluations using different criteria
    - relationship record with multiple rightful principals
    - ordinary task where no character or Agent should be created
    - requested public exposure without consent or authorization
    - connected Yawnbots with incompatible beliefs and privacy policies
  success: >
    A person can begin naturally, understand what the system thinks it heard,
    correct it cheaply, inspect why any Judgment was made, distinguish draft
    from action and action from Consequence, and provision only the bounded
    expression they intend without losing authorship.
  falsifier: >
    The workbench increases false certainty, modeling burden, compulsive
    completion, surveillance pressure, accidental publication, identity
    reification, or action errors compared with a simpler source-linked note.
